==Russian==

===Etymology===
Per Shansky and Tsyganenko akin to {{m|ru|чужо́й}}. Per Vasmer relation with the term is secondary. Compare typologically {{m|ru|дичь}} (akin to {{m|ru|ди́кий}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-чушь.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+||f|n=sg}}

# {{lb|ru|colloquial|often|pejorative}} [[rubbish]]
#: {{syn|ru|чушня́|дичь|вздор|бред}}
#: {{coi|ru|[[нести́]] '''чушь'''|to [[talk]] [[nonsense|'''nonsense''']]}}
#: {{coi|ru|'''чушь''' [[собачий|соба́чья]]|[[completely]] [[absurd]], [[codswallop]], all '''nonsense''', [[absolute]] [[bosh|'''bosh''']], [[damned]] '''nonsense''', a bunch of crap}}

